er;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$5.8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:2pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$(0.8)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:2pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$(0.7)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Year to date June&#160;30, 2026, Evergy Kansas Central made cash pension contributions of $29.0 million. Evergy Kansas Central expects to make additional cash pension contributions of $16.4 million in 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Year to date June&#160;30, 2026, Evergy Kansas Central made no post-retirement benefit contributions. Evergy Kansas Central does not expect to make contributions to the post-retirement benefit plans in 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;SHORT-TERM BORROWINGS AND SHORT-TERM BANK LINES OF CREDIT (NOTE 5)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In June 2026, Evergy entered into a $3.5 billion master credit facility which expires in June 2031. Evergy Kansas Central's borrowing capacity under the master credit facility is subject to a sublimit that can be unilaterally adjusted by Evergy, provided the sublimit remains within minimum and maximum sublimits as specified in the facility. The applicable interest rates and commitment fees of the facility are also subject to changes in ratings by the credit rating agencies. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;A default by Evergy Kansas Central or one of its significant subsidiaries on other indebtedness totaling more than $150.0 million constitutes a default by Evergy Kansas Central under the facility. Under the terms of this facility, Evergy Kansas Central is required to maintain a total indebtedness to total capitalization ratio, as defined in the facility, of not greater than 0.65 to 1.00 at all times. As of June&#160;30, 2026, Evergy Kansas Central was in compliance with this covenant. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In June 2026, contemporaneously with the entry into the new master credit facility, Evergy terminated its existing $2.5 billion master credit facility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The following table summarizes Evergy Kansas Central's borrowing capacity and short-term borrowings under the respective master credit facilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;t